From: ThorOS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: keep QinQ and PPPoE encapsulation exact

Use one bounded decoder for IPv4/IPv6 lookup, inet and legacy xt dispatch. Treat VLAN
metadata and inline 802.1Q/802.1AD as one two-tag budget, allow terminal PPPoE,
and leave malformed, unsupported or short packets with the normal stack.

Match both VLAN TPIDs; validate complete encapsulation stacks before emitting
any action, reserve action capacity atomically, and push the tuple stack in
reverse order. The flow tuple is wire-order, not forward-path order. Widen
only the encapsulation storage and ingress bitmap needed for two tags plus
PPPoE, and keep the existing 24-action maximum. Use the current network
header while removing PPPoE after inline VLANs, not the original MAC offset.

--- a/include/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table.h
+++ b/include/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table.h
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
